            'body'     => "## The mistake that costs the most\nAn agent hears silence after a price and rushes to fill it with a discount. The caller learns two things instantly: the price was never real, and if they wait, it will fall again.\n\n> 🎯 After you say the price — **say nothing.** Count to five in your head. Let them respond first.\n\n## Build the value stack\nBefore the number, list what is inside it. After the number, stop.\n\n» That includes the horse, a certified trainer, the helmet and body protector, the arena, and the whole level syllabus — so it works out to about ₹— a session.\n\n## Compare sideways, never down\nParents are not comparing you with another academy. They are comparing you with everything else they could spend that money on.\n\n» Most families tell us it costs about the same as a month of coaching classes — except this one is outdoors, off screens, and they actually beg to go.\n\n## When a discount IS right\n- The academy has an offer genuinely running — use it as the **closing** nudge, never the opener\n- A family enrols more than one rider together\n- They are upgrading to a longer package — the per-session rate already improves, so **sell that**, do not invent a new discount\n\n!> Never invent a discount to save a call. It is unfair to the riders who paid full price, and the moment word travels your price list means nothing.",
