            'takeaway' => 'Ask for the referral at the moment of maximum happiness, not at renewal time.',
            'body'     => "## The cheapest lead you will ever get\nA referred lead already trusts us before you say a word. They are quicker to close, less price-sensitive and they stay longer.\n\n## Ask at peak happiness\nNot at renewal. Not when chasing a payment. Ask **right after something good happens**:\n\n- 🏅 They finish a course and get the certificate\n- 🎉 A session goes brilliantly and the parent is beaming\n- ⬆️ The trainer clears them to move up a level\n\n» I am so glad she loves it. Most of our riders come through friends — is there anyone in her class who would enjoy this? I would happily keep them a visit slot.\n\n## Multiply within the family\nOne enquiry is rarely one rider:\n\n- 👧 **Siblings** — \"Does she have a brother or sister who would want to try?\"\n- 👩 **The parent** — adults ride too, and a parent watching every week is a warm lead sitting in your viewing area\n- 🎂 **Birthday groups** — a group of friends riding together is several leads in one visit\n\n> 🎯 Ask every single parent watching from the sidelines whether they have ever ridden. It is the single most under-used question on the premises.\n\n## Make referring easy\nSend them something forwardable — a short message with the booking link, not a speech.\n\n{join}\n\n!> Never offer a referral reward the academy has not approved. Enthusiasm is not authority.",
