        [
            'title'    => 'Honest urgency & scarcity',
            'emoji'    => '⏳',
            'takeaway' => 'Only use urgency that is true. Fake scarcity works once and costs you forever.',
            'body'     => "## Real urgency we genuinely have\n- 🪑 **Batch seats are first come, first served** — this is simply true, so say it\n- 📅 **A live offer with a real end date** — {offer}\n- 🌤️ **Season and school holidays** — batches genuinely fill before the holidays\n- 🐴 **Beginner horses are limited** — there are only so many suitable horses in a batch\n\n» Seats in a batch go in the order bookings come in, so the earlier you visit, the more choice you have over timings.\n\n## Urgency that is a lie\n- ❌ \"Only 2 seats left!\" when you have no idea\n- ❌ \"The offer ends tonight\" when it does not\n- ❌ \"The price is going up next week\" when nobody said so\n\n> 🎯 A caller who books because of a lie you told will find out. Then they tell other parents. Riding communities are small and they talk.\n\n## The honest version of pressure\nThe strongest pressure is not scarcity at all — it is **momentum**.\n\n» You are clearly keen, and honestly the hardest part is just getting here the first time. Let us get the visit done this weekend while everyone is enthusiastic — after that it is easy.\n\n## Silence as a tool\nAsk for the booking, then stop talking. The pause does more work than any deadline. Most agents cannot bear five seconds of silence and talk themselves straight back out of the sale.\n\n!> If you would be embarrassed for your manager to hear the reason you gave for hurrying, do not give it.",
        ],
        [
            'title'    => 'Your numbers — what good looks like',
