            'takeaway' => 'You cannot improve what you do not measure. Know your own conversion rate this week.',
            'body'     => "## The four numbers you own\n1. 📞 **Calls made** — activity. The one number entirely within your control.\n2. 📅 **Visits booked** — from calls. This is the real skill measure.\n3. 🏇 **Visits that turned up** — measures your confirmation habit, nothing else.\n4. 💰 **Riders joined & revenue** — the outcome.\n\nYour team page shows all four against your monthly target. Look at it **daily**, not on the last day of the month.\n\n## Where to look when a number is weak\n- **Calls low** → an activity problem. Work the overdue queue first thing each morning.\n- **Calls fine, visits low** → a *closing* problem. Re-read the Call Script module, especially the close.\n- **Visits booked, nobody turns up** → a *confirmation* problem. Send the day-before message, every time.\n- **Visits happen, nobody joins** → a *follow-up* problem. Message the same day, while it is still fresh.\n\n> 💡 This diagnosis is the most useful page in the whole course. One weak number tells you exactly which module to revisit.\n\n## The compounding habit\nOne extra call a day is roughly twenty-five extra calls a month. At even a modest conversion rate that is several extra riders a year, from a habit that costs four minutes a day.\n\n## Protect your reputation\nThe agent who is trusted outsells the agent who is clever — every year, without exception. Do what you said you would do, when you said you would do it.\n\n!> Never inflate your numbers by logging calls you did not make or visits you did not book. It is instantly visible in the reports, and it is the fastest way out of this job.",
